# Secrets — never commit.
#
# "secrets/" without the leading slash would also match internal/secrets, which
# is the package that manages the master key rather than a place one is kept.
# A clone then builds nothing and the reason is invisible: git says only that
# the directory is ignored. Anchor it.
/secrets/
*.key
*.pem
*.token
.env

# Build output
/dist/

# Go
*.test
*.out

# The UI harness writes these while it runs
tools/uicheck/.server.pid
